WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.720
Welcome to DBL Group's TalentHub!

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.560
This video is for the Factory HR team.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.840
You have three main jobs in TalentHub;
let's go through them one by one.

4
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:17.270
First, when a requisition is raised
in your unit it comes to you first:

5
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:23.230
you write the Job Analysis,
then approval begins.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:28.950
Second, once the job is posted, you send
the CVs you collect to the recruiter.

7
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:34.427
Third, you run the first interview for
the candidates the recruiter sends you.

8
00:00:34.777 --> 00:00:37.877
Approving requisitions,
setting salaries or offers,

9
00:00:37.997 --> 00:00:42.137
and running the recruiter's whole
pipeline are not part of this role.

10
00:00:42.487 --> 00:00:44.527
The role is given per unit;

11
00:00:44.647 --> 00:00:49.647
for access, contact the
Head of Talent Acquisition.

12
00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:55.847
If a unit has several Factory HR users,
they all share one Job Analysis queue.

13
00:00:56.197 --> 00:00:59.797
Sign in with your official DBL email
and password. The first time,

14
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:05.477
your password is your Employee Code;
set your own after signing in.

15
00:01:05.827 --> 00:01:10.587
In the menu: Requisitions,
for the Job Analysis.

16
00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:14.667
Assigned Candidates appears when
the recruiter sends you candidates,

17
00:01:15.587 --> 00:01:18.507
and My Interviews lists your interviews.

18
00:01:19.587 --> 00:01:23.827
Beside the bell is the Availability
button, for when you go on leave.

19
00:01:24.177 --> 00:01:26.937
Your first job: the Job Analysis.

20
00:01:27.377 --> 00:01:32.297
When a requisition is submitted in your
unit, every Factory HR there is notified,

21
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:35.737
and any of you can start.

22
00:01:35.857 --> 00:01:40.257
In Requisitions, open the one
with the Job Analysis status.

23
00:01:40.607 --> 00:01:42.967
The Job Analysis tab has two parts:

24
00:01:43.087 --> 00:01:49.047
Section A, what the raiser gave,
and Section B, yours,

25
00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:55.327
with four fields to fill. Last worked
on by shows who touched it last.

26
00:01:55.677 --> 00:02:00.597
Spot a mistake in Section A?
Click Edit vacancy information.

27
00:02:00.957 --> 00:02:04.597
You can fix the post,
department, numbers or dates;

28
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:09.117
every change is kept in History,
and the approval chain stays as it is.

29
00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:12.907
Now the writing, and AI helps here.

30
00:02:13.027 --> 00:02:18.307
Click Draft with AI and it reads the
requisition and drafts all four fields:

31
00:02:18.427 --> 00:02:22.889
Job Description, Education & Training,
Experience and Others.

32
00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:28.667
Always read and correct
it before you submit.

33
00:02:29.017 --> 00:02:33.522
Job Description takes the main duties,
Education & Training the qualifications,

34
00:02:33.642 --> 00:02:38.657
Experience the years needed,
and Others any extra conditions.

35
00:02:38.777 --> 00:02:41.897
As an example,
let's add a line to Experience.

36
00:02:42.247 --> 00:02:46.687
Any extra document goes
in Attachments as a PDF.

37
00:02:46.987 --> 00:02:50.967
Do it before you submit;
files can't be added afterwards.

38
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:53.677
Need to stop halfway?

39
00:02:53.797 --> 00:02:58.677
Click Save. You, or another Factory HR
in your unit, can pick it up right there.

40
00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:03.388
If the requisition itself has a problem,
use Return to raiser.

41
00:03:03.508 --> 00:03:06.268
Write what needs fixing
and click Send back.

42
00:03:06.947 --> 00:03:10.787
Once the raiser fixes and resends it,
it returns to your queue.

43
00:03:11.137 --> 00:03:14.717
When everything is right,
click Submit for approval. The

44
00:03:14.837 --> 00:03:19.617
status becomes Pending Approval, and the
first approver in the chain is notified.

45
00:03:19.967 --> 00:03:25.207
Good to know: if a unit has no Factory HR,
or all of you are on leave,

46
00:03:25.327 --> 00:03:28.927
the Head of Talent Acquisition
and the recruiters do the Job Analysis.

47
00:03:29.277 --> 00:03:35.397
Your second job: sending CVs to the
recruiter. Once the job is posted,

48
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:40.997
the requisition's Profile & Posting
tab has Send CVs to the recruiter,

49
00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:46.557
with the public job link, Share job link
and a ready Social post for Facebook.

50
00:03:46.907 --> 00:03:52.209
To send CVs, first choose the Source,
where they came from.

51
00:03:52.329 --> 00:03:56.667
For Employee Referral,
you pick the employee who referred them.

52
00:03:57.017 --> 00:04:00.737
Now add the CV PDFs, up to thirty at once.

53
00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:05.297
Names are taken from the file names;
correct any that are wrong.

54
00:04:05.657 --> 00:04:08.457
Then click Send CVs.

55
00:04:08.807 --> 00:04:13.407
The CVs reach the recruiter as Applied,
with your name on them.

56
00:04:13.847 --> 00:04:18.767
The list below shows whom you sent
and how often they've applied before.

57
00:04:19.287 --> 00:04:22.567
The recruiter decides who is shortlisted.

58
00:04:22.917 --> 00:04:25.357
Your third job: the first interview.

59
00:04:26.277 --> 00:04:29.517
When the recruiter uses Send
for interview you're notified,

60
00:04:29.637 --> 00:04:32.717
and Assigned Candidates
appears in the menu.

61
00:04:32.837 --> 00:04:35.877
Only the candidates sent to you are there.

62
00:04:36.227 --> 00:04:42.347
Five columns. To schedule: no time yet.
Scheduled: the time is set.

63
00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:48.427
Decision due: interviewed,
decision pending.

64
00:04:48.547 --> 00:04:52.747
With HR Head: with the HR Head.

65
00:04:53.587 --> 00:04:55.267
Done: finished.

66
00:04:55.617 --> 00:04:59.817
Interviewing two at once? Tick both,

67
00:04:59.937 --> 00:05:06.337
then Schedule 2 selected. With nobody
ticked, Schedule all takes everyone.

68
00:05:06.687 --> 00:05:12.247
Set the date and time,
always Bangladesh time, GMT plus six.

69
00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.887
Online creates a Google
Meet link by itself.

70
00:05:15.007 --> 00:05:18.287
In person, choose the Location
and type the room.

71
00:05:18.637 --> 00:05:24.397
The panel has two groups: From HR
Department and From other departments.

72
00:05:24.517 --> 00:05:28.357
The HR panelist also fills in the
candidate's salary and benefits.

73
00:05:29.197 --> 00:05:34.277
Below: Google Calendar and Email for
the candidate, Notify for the panel.

74
00:05:35.197 --> 00:05:36.637
Now click Schedule.

75
00:05:36.987 --> 00:05:41.667
On the day, the card asks:
Did this interview happen?

76
00:05:41.787 --> 00:05:47.267
Came: Interviewed. Didn't:
Did not attend. A mistake? Undo.

77
00:05:47.866 --> 00:05:50.907
Once anyone has marked,
Did not attend goes away.

78
00:05:51.257 --> 00:05:53.617
To change the time, Reschedule.

79
00:05:54.137 --> 00:05:59.707
The candidate gets the old and new times
by email, and the panel's links stay the

80
00:05:59.827 --> 00:06:02.527
same. Once someone has marked,
it can't be rescheduled.

81
00:06:02.647 --> 00:06:07.887
You mark two tests, Written Test
and Computer Literacy Test; the system

82
00:06:08.007 --> 00:06:14.607
scores the AI Proficiency Test itself.
Enter the marks for those that apply.

83
00:06:15.447 --> 00:06:20.727
Once saved, a mark is locked for you;
if it's wrong, tell the recruiter.

84
00:06:21.077 --> 00:06:24.787
Once the panel has marked,
the candidate moves to Decision due.

85
00:06:24.907 --> 00:06:26.558
Click Decide.

86
00:06:26.678 --> 00:06:32.677
Yes sends them to your unit’s HR Head if
there is one, otherwise straight to Final.

87
00:06:33.027 --> 00:06:36.939
Not taking them forward?
Choose No; a reason is required.

88
00:06:37.059 --> 00:06:42.587
Ticking Also send the regret
mail sends DBL's regret letter,

89
00:06:42.707 --> 00:06:47.816
only once, and never by itself.

90
00:06:48.166 --> 00:06:53.326
To send several at once,
use Send finalists to HR Head.

91
00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:58.326
The HR Head gets everyone in one email
and can decide from there.

92
00:06:58.676 --> 00:07:04.236
Going on leave? The round button
beside the bell: green means Available,

93
00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:09.036
amber means Away. Click it,
choose three, seven or fifteen days

94
00:07:09.156 --> 00:07:14.276
or your own last day,
add a note if you like, and Confirm leave.

95
00:07:14.626 --> 00:07:18.746
While you're Away you leave
the Job Analysis queue:

96
00:07:18.866 --> 00:07:23.706
no notifications,
and waiting work drops off your list.

97
00:07:24.666 --> 00:07:26.045
Your colleagues carry on.

98
00:07:26.395 --> 00:07:30.555
Back early? Click the button
and choose I'm back.

99
00:07:30.675 --> 00:07:34.635
Otherwise the system makes you
Available again when your leave ends.

100
00:07:34.985 --> 00:07:39.585
You're notified when a new
requisition arrives for Job Analysis,

101
00:07:39.705 --> 00:07:42.745
a raiser resends one,
the recruiter sends you candidates,

102
00:07:42.865 --> 00:07:47.225
the HR Head decides,
or an interview is set or moved.

103
00:07:47.575 --> 00:07:50.495
For email too, keep Email notifications on

104
00:07:50.615 --> 00:07:53.495
under the Notifications tab in Settings.

105
00:07:53.845 --> 00:07:57.565
Can you finish a Job
Analysis a colleague started?

106
00:07:58.405 --> 00:08:01.581
Of course. Anyone in the unit can;

107
00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:06.125
Last worked on by shows
who worked on it last,

108
00:08:06.405 --> 00:08:08.565
and every change is in History.

109
00:08:08.915 --> 00:08:14.315
Files can't be added after you submit;
ask the Head of Talent Acquisition if

110
00:08:14.835 --> 00:08:17.915
one is needed.
To correct a test mark you gave,

111
00:08:18.035 --> 00:08:20.675
ask the recruiter
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

112
00:08:21.025 --> 00:08:24.985
In short. One:
Job Analysis from Requisitions,

113
00:08:25.105 --> 00:08:29.265
start with Draft with AI,
finish with Submit for approval.

114
00:08:29.615 --> 00:08:33.535
Two: send CVs from Profile & Posting,
with the Source chosen.

115
00:08:33.885 --> 00:08:38.365
Three: interviews, attendance
and decisions in Assigned Candidates.

116
00:08:38.715 --> 00:08:44.915
Don't forget Availability before leave.
The full guide is a PDF under Tutorials;

117
00:08:45.435 --> 00:08:48.795
for sign-in trouble,
the IT Helpdesk. Thank you.

